# ---- .NET / F# (hdl/) ----
# Scoped to hdl/ on purpose: a bare `bin/` also matches Rust's src/bin
# convention, which is where runtime/host keeps its board binaries — real
# source that would silently stop being tracked.
hdl/**/bin/
hdl/**/obj/

# Packed .nupkg/.snupkg staged for a release push — built, never committed.
hdl/artifacts/
/packages/
riderModule.iml
/_ReSharper.Caches/
# The zenoh-c native library: a 30 MB platform binary, downloaded rather than
# vendored. See hdl/Warp11.GolView/README.md for the fetch.
zenohc/
zenohc.zip

# ---- Rust (runtime/) ----
target/
Cargo.lock

# ---- Vivado project artifacts (regenerated by hardware/vivado/build_*.tcl) ----
vivado.jou
vivado.log
vivado_*.backup.jou
vivado_*.backup.log
hardware/vivado/build_*.log
hardware/vivado/*_axi/
.Xil/
*.str
.cxl.*
hardware/vivado/*/*.cache/
hardware/vivado/*/*.gen/
hardware/vivado/*/*.hw/
hardware/vivado/*/*.ip_user_files/
hardware/vivado/*/*.runs/
hardware/vivado/*/*.sim/
hardware/vivado/*/*.srcs/
hardware/vivado/*/*.xpr

# Emitted Verilog, written by each F# project's `-- hardware <repo-root>`.
# Build output: Vivado sources it directly, and it is regenerated, not edited.
# The generated Rust register maps that come out of the same command ARE
# committed, under runtime/core/src — they are a compile-time dependency of
# the runtime crate, so emit-before-compile would otherwise be circular.
hardware/build/
# xmutil packaging output (bootgen .bit.bin, dtc .dtbo), per app.
hardware/xmutil/build/

# ---- editors, tooling, local state ----
.idea
.DS_Store
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/settings.local.json.tmp.*
.venv/
/warp11_backup.zip

# the static site is built, never committed
site/out/
site/apibuild/

# ---- Node, and only for the deploy tool ----
# `site/` holds wrangler as a project-local dev dependency rather than a global
# install, so the version that deploys the site is pinned and reviewable. That
# means package.json and package-lock.json ARE committed — the lockfile is the
# whole point — and only the installed tree is ignored.
site/node_modules/

# ---- Rider ----
# Per-user IDE state, one file per developer.
*.DotSettings.user

# Internal working notes and the agent brief. Kept out of the public repo until
# they have been read through for anything that should not be published — the
# working record is written for us, not for a reader arriving cold.
#
# Note that ignoring them is not the same as removing them: both were tracked,
# so they leave the index via `git rm -r --cached` and leave *history* only via
# a rewrite. Both were done together; ignoring alone would have published them.
/notes/
/CLAUDE.md

# Vivado's own logs and journals. Build output — they carry absolute paths from
# whoever ran the build, and say nothing a reader needs.
hardware/vivado/*.log
hardware/vivado/*.jou

# fsdocs' incremental cache. Regenerated by `dotnet fsdocs build`.
.fsdocs/
